    "text": "Cobalt chloride when dissolved in water forms pink colored complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> which has octahedral geometry. This solution on treating with cone <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> forms deep blue complex, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> which has a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> geometry. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math>, respectively, are",
