    "text": "<p>Cobalt chloride when dissolved in water forms pink coloured is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;.&nbsp;This is due to the electronic transition of an electron from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;energy level of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;complex. When excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>&nbsp;is added to the solution&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is transformed into deep blue colour complex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub></math></p><p>Tetrahedral complexes have smaller crystal field splitting than octahedral complexes.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><munder><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace></munder></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>Conc</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></mrow></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Tetrahedral</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
